 "verdict": "PARTLY_REAL_WIND_IS_COSMETIC",
 "verdict_detail": "MIXED, and the manuscript must say so. Home site reached the simulation and produced trajectory differences far larger than repeating one spec does, so the flights ARE distinct conditions along that axis. Wind did NOT: SIM_WIND_SPD is stored and read back correctly, but a vehicle holding position at 12 m/s tilts no more than one at 0 m/s, so no wind force is applied in this build. WP-C6 claimed variation along two axes and had one. The campaign is not one condition replicated 24 times, but it is less varied than it was described as being.",
 "what_gate_identity_means": "The injection is scripted to a fixed layer time and the simulated receiver responds to it with a fixed latency, so the gate trace is the same function of time in every flight regardless of where the vehicle is or what the wind is doing. That is a real property of a deterministic injection against a deterministic receiver model, and it means the bootstrap over flights has nothing to resample. It is not evidence that the flights are identical.",
 "why_it_blocks": "If the parameters never reached the simulator the WP-C6 campaign is one condition replicated 24 times and every interval derived from it is wrong."
}